2|0@stevenuniverse^1440140095#cuaf0hx:Barakid$:Sex and gender were the same interchangeable word untill recently, so sex as definition of gender was used in the creation of a lot of sexual words like Homosexual, heterosexual and asexual which would break down to same gender attraction, opposite gender attraction and no/null gender attraction. I don't know how many fucking times I'll have to argue this point but penises are male and Vaginas are female!!!!! The whole reason for the biological expression of gender/sex is because you have ovaries/vagina that produce estrogen and thus create feminine actions AND mental formation AND physical changes like breasts and voice changes. Males testicals produce testosterone that do the same, GENDER is biological and certainly linked 100% to genitals. Now you stated that genitals don't play a role is sexual arousal or attraction but they do, just maybe not the same way, gay people could use testosterone or estrogen in their formation of sexual attraction, they aren't sure yet but sex and attraction are all linked to hormones that are linked to genitals. 
0|0@stevenuniverse^1440159507#cuakdzn:Earthward-Bound$:Gender is a social construct. It's not a biological thing by any stretch of the imagination. What's biological is one's sex. Gender's just a way of categorizing people, so that one can predict certain behaviors and assign roles to those people based on the category that they're in. It was originally connected to sex because it was an enforcer for sexism. As societies move away from sexism, gender's become a way for people to define themselves. When people choose to assign their own gender, they have no reason to connect it to their genitals. And there's nothing about having a penis or a vagina that guarantees anything about sexuality or behavior. The basic idea behind masculinity and femininity is that if you're born with one sex, you'll be prone to certain things, and you'll be attracted to the opposite sex. But if being born with a particular sex doesn't guarantee that you're attracted to the opposite sex, the idea that it would define any other part of your identity is laughable. And I didn't say that you didn't need genitals to feel sexual attraction. I said that you didn't need genitals to be gay. Romantic attraction to someone presenting the same gender as you is still incredibly gay. The gems seem to display sexual desires, or at least, Rose did. I suspect amethyst as well, since she likes eating ans sleeping But if gems can learn to enjoy eating and sleeping, both of which are unnatural and unnecessary for them, it shouldn't be a stretch to see them developing a sexual appetite. Especially when we're talking about rose, who's picked up multiple human lovers over the past 5,000 years.
1|0@stevenuniverse^1440229906#cubmb22:Barakid$:I think your confusing gender with personality. Sorry but they are not one in the same. You can change how you act and portray yourself however you like, your gender however IS biologically linked and is interchangeable with the word sex in my opinion. Gender is defined as **the state of being male or female** by merriam-webster or as gendered words in some languages, which also happen to correlate with femininity and masculinity or neuter gender. So whatever you think you mean by gender its wrong, you certainly can change your look, actions and mannerisms but that has nothing to do with biological gender aside from the effects of testosterone and estrogen hormones on cognitive and physical functions. Changing the way you dress and speak is not a new gender its changing your personality. Now that isn't to say I disagree with transexuality, I simply hate that people are being told that if one THINKS they are female or male that everyone has to believe its so, even though they are biologically still female or male, you can't just disregard science like that, A lot of transexuals go threw a transition using hormone therapy, which actualy DOES change the biological expression of gender, but wanting to be something doesn't just make it so, me wanting green eyes doesn't mean they will just become that, DNA and biological sex exists blatantly you can't just pretend its not there and make-up whatever gender means to you, science is science. 
